Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["RewriteEventEvolution", "ObjectName",
 CellID->987282728,ExpressionUUID->"5fdeed31-391d-f845-a503-7cea660ff925"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"bb702044-4074-3746-9c7d-887ccb62b6f6"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["RewriteEventEvolution",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->
     "paclet:SamuelFrerichs/StructureAdaptiveEvolution/ref/\
RewriteEventEvolution"], 
   RowBox[{"[", 
    RowBox[{"rule", ",", " ", "state", ",", " ", "limits"}], "]"}]}]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"075dc069-7b7d-184e-add8-f2b7f5e39673"],
 " \[LineSeparator]",
 "runs a single-way evolution of the rule or rule set ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["rule", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "62f01286-ce84-1b4a-bb6a-d3ca4325a470"],
 " from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["state", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "63826e07-5f42-704c-83b1-f929b658bd50"],
 " with explicit event and edge identities, and gives its events, edge \
records, states, final state, status and causal graph."
}], "Usage",
 CellID->488809598,ExpressionUUID->"a7de67db-bf6e-4e4e-8c59-0179c44ccee5"],

Cell["\<\
The option \"UpdateOrder\" chooses the events of each step. \"Generational\" \
(the default) applies a maximal set of pairwise edge-disjoint events \
simultaneously, picked greedily in (generation, rule, consumed edge IDs) \
order; under \"VertexDeletion\" semantics it applies one event per step. The \
other orders apply one event per step: \"Sequential\" the least by (rule \
index, consumed edge IDs), \"LeastRecent\" the one consuming the oldest \
edges, \"MostRecent\" the one consuming the newest edges, and {\"Random\", s} \
one chosen by a private generator seeded by {s, step}, which leaves the \
session's random state untouched. The option \"IncludeInitialEvent\" (False) \
adds an initial event that creates the initial edges.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->249635076,ExpressionUUID->"550353a1-9405-7346-9661-b1eeefb1a046"],

Cell["\<\
Every event has an \"EventID\", \"Step\", \"Generation\", \"RuleIndex\" and \
the IDs of its \"Inputs\" and \"Outputs\" edges. \"Rule\" is the rule that \
was evolved. \"EdgeRecords\" gives for every edge ID its edge, generation, \
creator event (0 for initial edges) and destroyer event. In the unordered \
universe a duplicate edge is merged into its oldest copy and records Missing[\
\"MergedInto\", id].\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->615890453,ExpressionUUID->"b85ad8bf-2d52-c943-a4d9-c5400947c7a2"],

Cell["\<\
The causal graph has one vertex per event and an edge from the event that \
created an edge to each event that consumed it. Status is \"Terminated\" when \
no event applies, otherwise a cap status.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->867614823,ExpressionUUID->"92f1f24f-83c0-ff4f-a655-101bdf73efaf"],

Cell["\<\
Evolution limits are an Association with the keys \"MaxGenerations\" (default \
10), \"MaxEvents\" (1000), \"MaxStates\" (Infinity) and \"TimeConstraint\" \
(30. seconds); missing keys take their defaults.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->147088074,ExpressionUUID->"7a7eeeb6-83d3-1c43-a5a3-baa8828823c7"]
}, Open  ]],

